<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Seneca Nation</h1><p class="st-meta">1450 CE – present (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The largest nation of the Iroquois Confederacy, the Keepers of the Western Door, and birthplace of the Longhouse religion of Handsome Lake.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Seneca lived in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seneca-lake">Seneca Lake</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genesee-river">Genesee River</a>, the westernmost of the five founding <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/iroquois-confederacy">Haudenosaunee</a> nations. Joining the Iroquois <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/confederate-states-of-america">Confederacy</a> around the mid-15th century, according to tradition, they guarded its western flank, and towns such as Ganondagan grew into some of the largest settlements in the region.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Seneca sent eight chiefs to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-council-qing">Grand Council</a> and, as the most numerous nation, supplied many warriors in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beaver-wars">Beaver Wars</a> against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/huron-confederacy">Huron Confederacy</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/neutral-confederacy">Neutral Confederacy</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/erie-nation">Erie Nation</a>. In 1687 the French governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacques-rene-de-brisay-de-denonville">Denonville</a> burned Ganondagan. In the late 18th century the war chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornplanter">Cornplanter</a> and the orator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-jacket">Red Jacket</a> led the nation, and in 1799 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/handsome-lake">Handsome Lake</a> began the teaching that became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/longhouse-religion">Longhouse religion</a>.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>After siding with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>, the Seneca sold most of their lands in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-big-tree">Treaty of Big Tree</a> in 1797. In 1848 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allegany-reservation">Allegany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattaraugus-reservation">Cattaraugus</a> communities formed the Seneca Nation of Indians, an elected republic, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tonawanda-band-of-seneca">Tonawanda</a> kept traditional chiefs. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinzua-dam">Kinzua Dam</a> flooded Allegany land in the 1960s.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/seneca-nation.jpg" alt="Seneca Nation" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Jacqueline Chandler · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FEMA_-_42287_-_FEMA_FCO_makes_an_award_in_New_York.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1450 CE – present (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Cornplanter, Red Jacket, Handsome Lake</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Haudenosaunee traditional religion, Longhouse religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Seneca</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Onondowahgah, Seneca</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1738&amp;focus=seneca-nation" aria-label="Seneca Nation on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2767 665 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Seneca Nation lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3087 921L3160 908"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3160 908h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3087 921h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3087 921h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1738&amp;foc